{
  "_comment": [
    "5E powersets, structured. Authored from the legacy prose in public/templates/archtypes.json,",
    "which stated each power as a string with a hand-typed cost ('EB 10d6', cost '5u'). Here the",
    "costs are DERIVED: the engine prices each power from the template data, and the framework",
    "arithmetic (multipower ultra slots /10, elemental-control discount) falls out of the",
    "decorators. Nothing below states a cost.",
    "",
    "Shape is a .hdc `powers` block. The KEY is the framework type — normalizeCharacterData stamps",
    "originalType from it — and slots are siblings linked to their container by parentid.",
    "`ultraSlot: true` makes a multipower slot cost active/10 rather than active/5.",
    "",
    "A powerset may carry an `approximations` list naming any knowingly-loose corner and why —",
    "the legacy prose is sometimes vague, and being faithful to it beats inventing precision it",
    "never had. Declare them; approximations() lists every one for review and a test pins them.",
    "",
    "Force Wall length/height/body/width levels are bought ABOVE the base 2m x 2m wall, so 0",
    "means base size — a real, legal wall, not a wall with no extent. Its 50 active points are",
    "pure defence (10 rPD + 10 rED), which is exactly what the prose priced at 5u.",
    "",
    "See docs/RANDOM_CHARACTER.md. Verified against the allocator's balance in",
    "core/random/__tests__/powerset.test.ts."
  ],
